## 4. On-Page SEO Checklist

**Title Tags:** Each page should have a unique `<title>` tag that begins with its target keywords and accurately describes the content【47†L224-L232】. Keep titles descriptive and under ~60 characters (we use 70–80 char here for readability, but Google typically shows ~60【47†L224-L232】). Avoid keyword stuffing.  

**Meta Descriptions:** Add a `<meta name="description">` tag to every page. It should be a concise summary (120–160 chars) that includes key phrases and entices click-through【48†L1-L4】. Semrush advises keeping it “short and complete” (around 105 chars to avoid truncation【48†L1-L4】). Our examples above follow these guidelines.

**Header Tags:** Use **one H1** per page (as outlined above). H1 should include the main keyword and clearly describe the page【47†L253-L261】. Subheadings (H2, H3) break the content into logical sections (e.g. “Why This Conversion”, “Examples”, “FAQs”). The H1 can be slightly longer than the title tag and more descriptive【47†L253-L261】. Each H2 should also be descriptive and include secondary keywords where natural.

**Content Quality:** Ensure each page has explanatory content (not just the tool). We’ve provided sample paragraphs above. Keep paragraphs short (3-5 sentences) for readability. Explain local context (e.g. why people search these conversions in Pakistan). Use bullet lists or charts for clarity (as in the main page’s Land Units section). Naturally include keywords in the text, especially early on (without stuffing). 

**Keyword Frequency:** Avoid repeating the exact keyword too much; use synonyms (“sq ft”, “square feet”). Focus on variations (e.g. “square feet”, “sq ft”, “plot size” for Marla pages). Integrate terms naturally in first 100 words where possible【47†L265-L273】.

**Internal Links:** From each page, link to related conversions to keep users on-site and distribute authority. For example, each page’s “Related Guides” links back to the main converter and other relevant tools. Ensure the main converter page links to all subpages and vice versa, forming a tight internal network. Use descriptive anchor text (e.g. link text “Marla to Square Feet” to that guide). Google’s guidelines emphasize linking related pages to help crawling【42†L463-L472】 (straight URL guidance implies this).

**Canonical URLs:** Use a self-referencing canonical link in the `<head>` of each page (e.g. `<link rel="canonical" href="https://error4am.github.io/land-converter/kanal-to-square-feet/" />`). This avoids any duplicate content issues. All URLs should be lowercase, hyphen-separated (no spaces or underscores) as recommended【42†L521-L529】. For example, use `/5-marla-in-square-feet/` (not underscores or capitals)【42†L521-L529】.

**URL Structure:** The URLs are already logical. If creating new pages, use the format `land-converter/[topic-name]`. For example, “kanal-to-square-feet”, “5-marla-in-square-feet”. Use hyphens between words【42†L521-L529】. Avoid changing these slugs since they are already indexed.

**Page Speed & Mobile:** Ensure the site is mobile-friendly and fast (GitHub Pages is typically fast). Compress images and use responsive design. Google’s PageSpeed and Mobile-Friendly tests should pass. (This is assumed, but always worth checking after updates.)  

**Image and Alt Tags:** If any icons or graphs are used, add descriptive `alt` text (e.g. `alt="Marla to Square Feet conversion chart"`). Use `og:image` meta tags (see below) for social sharing images. No heavy images are needed for this content, but if adding an infographic or logo, optimize it.

**Schema Markup:** Add **FAQPage** JSON-LD for each page’s FAQs (see next section). This helps Google generate rich results【45†L450-L459】. Only use it for actual Q&A content on the page (as provided above). Test with Google’s Rich Results Test to ensure validity.

**Robots & Meta Tags:** In robots.txt or meta tags, allow crawling of all pages. For GitHub Pages, typically include:  
```
User-agent: *
Allow: /
Sitemap: https://error4am.github.io/land-converter/sitemap.xml
```  
In HTML head, use `<meta name="robots" content="index, follow">` on all pages to ensure indexing. No `noindex` tags needed since we want everything indexed.

**Duplicate Content:** Avoid duplicating paragraphs across pages. Each conversion page has unique content. The intro and FAQs differ per page. The main converter page has its own scope (covering all units). If reuse is needed, slightly rephrase.

**Breadcrumbs/Navigation:** Ensure the site navigation (Home/Guides/FAQ links at top) is clear. It helps users find related guides. The existing header links to Home, Guides, FAQ are good. If possible, add a breadcrumb or a header “Back to main converter” on subpages (already partly present).

**Monitoring:** After publishing changes, use Google Search Console to monitor impressions, clicks, CTR, and ranking positions for target keywords (we’ll create a tracking template below).

